SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Mosna with donkey races\, Agia Paraskevi
LOCATION:Agia Paraskevi\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The folklore society of Agia Paraskevi has run this two-day feast since 1985 at the chapel of Panagia Mosna\, 2.5 km above the village: on 22 August a garlanded calf is led through the village at midday\, society members ride decorated donkeys up to the chapel in the evening and the music goes all night\; on the 23rd there is liturgy\, blessed 'kiskek' (wheat and meat stew cooked overnight) for everyone\, donkey races at Ligaridia in the afternoon and dancing in the village square till dawn. The rural end of the summer for Lesvos\; book a table in the square.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-panagia-mosna-with-donkey-races-a
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-panagia-mosna-with-donkey-races-a
END:VEVENT
